{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 6 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 6 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nLittle Petya loves training spiders. Petya has a board n\u2009\u00d7\u2009m in size. Each cell of the board initially has a spider sitting on it. After one second Petya chooses a certain action for each spider, and all of them humbly perform its commands. There are 5 possible commands: to stay idle or to move from current cell to some of the four side-neighboring cells (that is, one command for each of the four possible directions). Petya gives the commands so that no spider leaves the field. It is allowed for spiders to pass through each other when they crawl towards each other in opposite directions. All spiders crawl simultaneously and several spiders may end up in one cell. Petya wants to know the maximum possible number of spider-free cells after one second.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 6 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class ProblemE {\n    static int width, height;\n    static final int INFINITY = 9999999;\n    static Set<Integer> patterns = new HashSet<Integer>();\n    \n    static void explore(int column, int row, int state) {\n        if (column >= width) {\n            patterns.add(state);\n            return;\n        }\n        if (row >= 1) {\n            explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<column));\n        }\n        if (row <= height - 2) {\n            explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<(column+width*2)));\n        }\n        if (column >= 1) {\n            explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<((column-1)+width)));\n        }\n        if (column <= width - 2) {\n            explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<((column+1)+width)));\n        }\n        explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<(column+width)));\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] input = reader.readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        width = Integer.parseInt(input[0]);\n        height = Integer.parseInt(input[1]);\n        if (width > height) {\n            int temp = width;\n            width = height;\n            height = temp;\n        }\n    \n        int[][] table = new int[height+1][1<<(width*3)];\n        for (int i = 0 ; i <= height ; i++) {\n            Arrays.fill(table[i], INFINITY);\n        }\n        table[0][0] = 0;\n        \n        for (int level = 0 ; level < height ; level++) {\n            patterns.clear();\n            explore(0, level, 0);\n            for (int prev = 0 ; prev < 1<<(width*2) ; prev++) {\n                if (table[level][prev] != INFINITY) {\n                    for (int pattern : patterns) {\n                        int combined = (pattern | prev);\n                        int shifted = combined >> width;\n                        int count = Integer.bitCount(combined & ((1<<width) - 1));\n                        table[level+1][shifted] = Math.min(table[level+1][shifted], table[level][prev] + count);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int minCost = INFINITY;\n        for (int finalState = 0 ; finalState < 1<<(width*2) ; finalState++) {\n            minCost = Math.min(minCost, table[height][finalState] + Integer.bitCount(finalState));\n        }\n        System.out.println(height * width - minCost);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class ProblemE {\n    static int width, height;\n    static final int INFINITY = 9999999;\n    static List<Integer> patterns = new ArrayList<Integer>();\n    \n    static void explore(int column, int row, int state) {\n        if (column >= width) {\n            patterns.add(state);\n            return;\n        }\n        // Stay in place\n        explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<(column+width)));\n        // Move up\n        if (row >= 1) {\n            explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<column));\n        }\n        // Move down\n        if (row <= height - 2) {\n            explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<(column+width*2)));\n        }\n        // Move left\n        if (column >= 1) {\n            explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<((column-1)+width)));\n        }\n        // Move right\n        if (column <= width - 2) {\n            explore(column+1, row, state|(1<<((column+1)+width)));\n        }\n    }\n    \n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader reader = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String[] input = reader.readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        width = Integer.parseInt(input[0]);\n        height = Integer.parseInt(input[1]);\n        if (width > height) {\n            int temp = width;\n            width = height;\n            height = temp;\n        }\n    \n        int[][] table = new int[height+1][1<<(width*2)];\n        for (int i = 0 ; i <= height ; i++) {\n            Arrays.fill(table[i], INFINITY);\n        }\n        table[0][0] = 0;\n        \n        for (int level = 0 ; level < height ; level++) {\n            patterns.clear();\n            explore(0, level, 0);\n            for (int prev = 0 ; prev < 1<<(width*2) ; prev++) {\n                if (table[level][prev] != INFINITY) {\n                    for (int pattern : patterns) {\n                        int combined = (pattern | prev);\n                        int shifted = combined >> width;\n                        int count = Integer.bitCount(combined & ((1<<width) - 1));\n                        if (table[level][prev] + count < table[level+1][shifted]) {\n                            table[level+1][shifted] = table[level][prev] + count;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int minCost = INFINITY;\n        for (int finalState = 0 ; finalState < 1<<(width*2) ; finalState++) {\n            if (table[height][finalState] != INFINITY) {\n                minCost = Math.min(minCost, table[height][finalState] + Integer.bitCount(finalState));\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(height * width - minCost);\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.85\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-1.1920928244535389e-07, -7.497983460780233e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, 0.0, -1.9430925021879375e-05, -1.2278481335670222e-05, -1.0132738680113107e-05, -5.602820692729438e-06, -1.490105023549404e-05, -1.7523612768854946e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.883488948806189e-05, -6.318072337307967e-06, -4.172316494077677e-06, -0.00020656836568377912, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -0.0002615109842736274, -0.000912250077817589, -0.0009152276325039566, -4.172316494077677e-06, -0.0005077026435174048, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -6.675497570540756e-05, -0.004626285284757614, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -0.00038115866482257843, -5.125986263010418e-06, -0.00018320789968129247, -1.0967194612021558e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -8.940656698541716e-06, -0.001